00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
Today on the Anime Zone, a review of Highschool of the Dead,

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.710
an anime about zombies.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.040
It's Japan's first take on the zombie apocalypse genre,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.920
following a group of survivors battling the vast army of
the undead with a cast of highly-trained supermodels,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.850
complete with over-the-top, balls-to-the-walls, physics-breaking action,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.820
as if the whole thing was programmed in the fucking Matrix.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.020
Speaking of The Matrix...

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.150
[Neo]
What are you trying to tell me?

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.860
That I can dodge bullets?

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:30.570
Whoa...

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:51.160
At this point in time, the zombie genre is a concept
that has been done to death in the Western media,

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.220
invading movies, comic books, video games, and even novels.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.900
It's gotten to the point that all we need to do to
advertise something is slap some zombies in it

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.960
and the thing will sell out as if it came
with complimentary biscuits and blowjobs.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.680
Surprisingly enough, there hasn't really been any
anime centered around a zombie apocalypse,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.280
even when the medium of anime gives the Japanese the
chance to play with new and original takes of existing genres,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.710
or explore imaginative settings that couldn't
have been presented in any other medium,

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.650
which would have been perfect for a re-imagining of the zombie genre.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.220
And then, along comes Highschool of the Dead,
a zombie apocalypse set in fucking high school.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.820
Shine on, Japan, shine the fuck on.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.060
Highschool of the Dead is a 2010 anime done by Studio Madhouse

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.810
and follows the progression of a zombie apocalypse
seen through the eyes of Takashi Komuro,

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.560
who's basically a clone of Kazuki from Buso Renkin, but then again,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.140
I'm pretty sure super-serious, spikey-haired high school
boy takes up around 90% of all anime protagonists.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.310
Anyway, one day, where Takashi is busy pondering why pinky
promises made in elementary school don't equal guaranteed sex,

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.610
and casually pretending to converse with a girl despite
the fact that her face is up here and not down there,

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:49.180
he bears witness to a zombie attack by what seems
to be a zombie version of Bill from accounting.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.030
From there on, panic ensues in school as everyone
gets involved in the massive biting-frenzy and,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.960
before you know it, the whole school has become
an infected pit of dead flesh before you can say,

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.190
"you've got red on you."

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:03.100
From here, Takashi must rise to the challenge
as he forms a rag-tag team of survivors

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.400
and faces the biggest challenge of his life:

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.540
trying to keep his fucking dick in his pants with a
bloody sex parade constantly waving in his face 24/7

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.870
