00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.320
The show plays out like your typical zombie survival story,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.360
with a group of unlikely heroes teaming
up to battle hordes of the undead

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.350
wearing short skirts that cover about a
millimeter of skin, while, along the way,

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.750
hinting at the fact that the real monster
in all of this is, instead, mankind itself.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.520
And, in the end, the cast is what you get if you cross a
zombie apocalypse with your typical harem-ecchi anime.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.540
You have Takashi, who starts off as the unwilling,
spikey-haired hero who is thrown into a situation

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.000
where he is forced to fight for survival and
transforms into the confident badass leader

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.200
who's not afraid to kick ass and take names, while occasionally
asserting his authority by bitch-slapping the odd girl;

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.480
